CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc_node(sizeof(*iommu)...) over kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct powerpc_iommu)...)
#114: FILE: arch/powerpc/kernel/iommu.c:717:
+	iommu = kzalloc_node(sizeof(struct powerpc_iommu), GFP_KERNEL,

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

